Package: tux-codec-dkms
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Tuxedo <tux@localhost>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: dkms (>= 3), gcc, make, linux-headers-arm64-16k
Description: Tuxedo video codec channel (/dev/hvcodec), as a DKMS module
 tux_codec drives Tuxedo's hvcodec device: each open file of /dev/hvcodec is
 a context of the host's video codecs, and raw frames go to and from the host
 from the caller's own pages, with no copy in the guest. libhvcodec (in
 tux-ffmpeg) uses it when it is there, and TCP to 10.0.2.4:8470 when not.
 The machine must run with the codec device on (tuxvm --vcodec-dma).
 .
 DKMS builds the module for each installed kernel with headers, and again
 after each kernel update. The module has no signature: the kernel accepts it
 and records a taint.
